% --- added 2026-07-29: the SZ cluster method for varying constants ---------
% The closest existing analogue to this paper's reconstructed-quantity rows, and
% previously uncited. The mechanism is the same one used here -- the Compton-y
% parameter carries sigma_T ~ alpha^2/m_e^2 -- and the standard observable is a
% reconstructed SZ quantity compared against an independent probe of the same gas
% (X-ray), which is structurally what the dispersion and Faraday rows do with a
